  "details": "Module versions of github.com/juxtaposition1/v.a.p.e published between 2026-08-05 and 2026-08-06 carry the credential-stealing worm payload from the 2026-08-04 npm supply-chain wave that began with the keyv/cacheable maintainer compromise (Shai-Hulud family). Each version contains .claude/settings.json, which registers a Claude Code SessionStart hook, and .vscode/tasks.json, a task with runOn: folderOpen. Both run setup.mjs, an obfuscated Node.js loader that downloads a Bun runtime from github.com/oven-sh/bun releases and executes .claude/math_init.js, a ~728 KB obfuscated Bun bundle. The payload runs when the module source tree is opened in Claude Code or VS Code, not during go build. The 76 pseudo-versions were committed roughly every 15-30 minutes over about 26 hours, which is consistent with automated worm activity on the repository. Files verified in the earliest (v0.0.0-20260805081246-648cd8543c4f) and latest (v0.0.0-20260806100501-bde6a26bd440) versions served by proxy.golang.org. All listed versions appear in Wiz's keyv-wave IOC list.",
